{{template "head" .}}

<section class="wrap section">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div>
      <h1>NSM Documentation &amp; Developer Reference</h1>
      <p class="muted">Complete guide to the NSM client, FXServer, Keymaster, in-app login, and local masterlist</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:8px">
      <a href="/keymaster" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Open Keymaster</a>
      <a href="/forum/c/server-dev" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Server Dev Forum</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-sidebar">
      <div class="docs-nav-box">
        <h4>Documentation</h4>
        <a href="#quickstart">1. Quick Start</a>
        <a href="#client-login">2. In-App Client Login</a>
        <a href="#keymaster">3. Keymaster &amp; Server Keys</a>
        <a href="#server-cfg">4. Server Configuration</a>
        <a href="#profiles">5. Custom User Profiles</a>
        <a href="#http-api">6. Masterlist &amp; Auth APIs</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="docs-main">
      <div class="doc-card" id="quickstart">
        <h3>1. Quick Start — Launching the Full NSM Stack</h3>
        <p class="muted">The NSM stack runs as a single self-contained platform (`NSM-Masterlist.exe`) alongside `nsm-server.exe` and `NSM.exe`:</p>
        <pre class="code">powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\START-LOCALHOST.ps1</pre>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:8px">
          `NSM-Masterlist.exe` binds `http://127.0.0.1:80` and provides the website (`/`), live server browser (`/servers`), Keymaster (`/keymaster`), community forum (`/forum`), custom profile system (`/account`, `/u/{username}`), and in-app client authentication (`/user-api-key/new`).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-card" id="client-login">
        <h3>2. Signing In Inside the NSM Desktop Client</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Clicking <strong>Sign In / Link Account</strong> in the NSM client navbar opens <code>http://127.0.0.1/user-api-key/new</code> in your browser instead of Discord.
        </p>
        <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0 18px;line-height:1.7">
          <li>Sign in (or create an account) on the authorization screen and click <strong>Authorize &amp; Sign In to NSM Client</strong>.</li>
          <li>The NSM website encrypts a persistent <code>User-Api-Key</code> using the client's RSA public key and delivers it via both <code>nsm://accept-auth?payload=...</code> and automatic local polling (<code>/api/auth/client-poll</code>).</li>
          <li>Your custom display name, avatar, and role badge sync directly into the NSM client navbar.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-card" id="keymaster">
        <h3>3. NSM Keymaster &amp; Server Keys (<code>/keymaster</code>)</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Create and manage cryptographic server keys in <a href="/keymaster">Keymaster</a>:
        </p>
        <pre class="code"># Add your Keymaster key to server-local.cfg or server.cfg:
sets sv_nsmServerKey "nsm_srv_..."</pre>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:8px">
          When your server sends its heartbeat to <code>POST /api/serverlist/ingress</code>, the masterlist verifies the key via constant-time iterated HMAC-SHA256, strips <code>sv_nsmServerKey</code> from public listings, and binds the endpoint to your account so no other account can overwrite it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-card" id="server-cfg">
        <h3>4. Connecting to a Server</h3>
        <pre class="code"># Click Connect on /servers, or press F8 inside NSM and run:
connect 127.0.0.1:30120</pre>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-card" id="profiles">
        <h3>5. Custom User Profiles &amp; Avatars (<code>/account</code> &amp; <code>/u/{username}</code>)</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Visit <a href="/account">Profile &amp; Settings</a> to upload a custom PNG/JPG/GIF avatar (or customize your generated monogram avatar color), set your display name, custom title, bio, banner color/image, location, Discord tag, and favorite server. Every user also has a public profile at <code>/u/{username}</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-card" id="http-api">
        <h3>6. HTTP API Reference</h3>
        <pre class="code">GET  /health                         # Stack readiness probe
GET  /api/servers/live               # Live JSON server list &amp; player counts
GET  /api/servers/streamRedir/       # Binary protobuf masterlist stream for NSM.exe
GET  /api/servers/single/{ep}        # Single server JSON details
POST /api/serverlist/ingress         # FXServer heartbeat ingress
GET  /keymaster                      # Keymaster Web Portal
POST /api/keymaster/issue            # Issue a new nsm_srv_... key
POST /api/keymaster/revoke           # Revoke an existing key
GET  /user-api-key/new               # NSM Client RSA User-Api-Key authorization
POST /api/auth/client-poll           # NSM Client automatic login poller
POST /l/api/validate/discourse       # Native legitimacy.dll Discourse identity check</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

